  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Fairy Bai Qing notes that many Immortal Crane Sect Gu Immortals were tied up in the reincarnation battlefield while the sect still failed to retake Hu Immortal blessed land.",
      "chapters": [
        696
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fairy_bai_qing",
        "fac_immortal_crane_sect",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "loc_hu_immortal_blessed_land"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In an Immortal Crane Sect meeting, Lei Tan says he has managed its affairs for over thirty years, reports a mid-year loss that was only partly recovered, and asks for a rank six Gu Immortal’s battle strength or three desolate beasts as reinforcement. He Feng Yang and Shu Zhi Ge argue that the other nine sects are competitors there, so pouring more force in only draws matching reinforcements; the immediate goal is to hold territory. The ten great ancient sects compete and station Gu Immortals on the battlefield.",
      "chapters": [
        697
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_lei_tan",
        "char_he_feng_yang"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After Immortal Crane Sect stabilizes the northwest, it is heavily suppressed there, and Lei Tan returns injured to recuperate. Reincarnation Battlefield is the publicly recognized number one battlefield killer move in the world, set up by Paradise Earth Immortal Venerable himself, with the ten great ancient sects controlling the area for many years in fierce competition.",
      "chapters": [
        745
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "origin-and-standing",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_paradise_earth_immortal_venerable",
        "fac_ten_great_sects"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Explorers of a Paradise Earth true inheritance test compare that illusion to Reincarnation Battlefield and say Paradise Earth Immortal Venerable created such killer moves to deal with the rank eight expert Combat Demon, with Reincarnation Battlefield as the peak of the series. After many years, Central Continent’s ten great ancient sects have nurtured countless Gu Immortal experts with it.",
      "chapters": [
        1651
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "purpose-and-training",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "inh_paradise_earth_true_inheritance",
        "fac_ten_great_ancient_sects"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Paradise Earth Immortal Venerable created Reincarnation Battlefield in Central Continent. The ten great ancient sects occupy that place and send Gu Immortals to fight inside it. Whoever dies inside does not lose their life, and only sustains some injuries or damage if they die too many times.",
      "chapters": [
        1889
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "death-rules",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_central_continent"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Among the ten venerables, Paradise Earth Immortal Venerable was the most skilled at using immortal battlefield killer moves, publicly known as number one among venerables in that aspect. Reincarnation Battlefield continues to exist in Central Continent and is owned by the ten great ancient sects.",
      "chapters": [
        2047
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "skill-and-ownership",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "He created it because he did not want bloodshed between Central Continent Gu Immortals, and used it to resolve their conflicts.",
      "chapters": [
        2059
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "conflict-resolution",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lu Wei Yin later states that Central Continent’s Paradise Earth true inheritance is Reincarnation Battlefield.",
      "chapters": [
        2087
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "inheritance-naming",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_lu_wei_yin"
      ]
    }
  ],
